.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.BI "int wordCount(FILE *" file ", int *" lines ", int *" words ", int *" chars ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wordCount()
reads the open file stream
.I file
from its current position to the end, and stores the number of lines,
words and characters in the variables pointed to by
.IR lines ,
.I words
and
.IR chars .
A line is counted for every newline character. A word is a sequence of
characters separated by spaces, tabs or newlines. The results match the
.BR wc (1)
command.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 if any argument is NULL.
